## Best Practices

### 1. Message History Management

Keep conversation history concise to avoid token limits:

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Last 10 messages
const recentMessages = conversationHistory.slice(-10);

// ❌ Bad: Entire history (may exceed token limit)
const allMessages = conversationHistory;
```

### 2. Error Handling

Always handle potential errors:

```typescript
try {
  const response = await fetch('/api/ai/chat', { /* ... */ });

  if (response.status === 429) {
    const retryAfter = response.headers.get('Retry-After');
    console.log(`Rate limited. Retry after ${retryAfter} seconds`);
    return;
  }

  if (!response.ok) {
    const error = await response.json();
    throw new Error(error.error);
  }

  const data = await response.json();
  // Process response...
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Chat error:', error.message);
}
```

### 3. Tool Calling Loop

When using tools, implement a proper execution loop:

```typescript
let messages = [{ role: 'user', content: 'Create a banner' }];

while (true) {
  const response = await fetch('/api/ai/chat', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: JSON.stringify({ messages, model, tools })
  });

  const data = await response.json();
  const choice = data.choices[0];

  if (choice.finish_reason === 'stop') {
    console.log('Final answer:', choice.message.content);
    break;
  }

  if (choice.finish_reason === 'tool_calls') {
    // Execute tools and add results to messages
    for (const toolCall of choice.message.tool_calls) {
      const result = await executeTool(toolCall);
      messages.push({
        role: 'tool',
        tool_call_id: toolCall.id,
        content: JSON.stringify(result)
      });
    }
  }
}
```

### 4. Model Selection

Choose models based on your use case:

| Use Case | Recommended Model |
|----------|-------------------|
| Simple Q&A | `google/gemini-2.0-flash-exp:free` |
| Complex Reasoning | `openai/gpt-5.1` |
| Code Generation | `anthropic/claude-3.5-sonnet` |
| Vision Analysis | `google/gemini-pro-1.5` |
| Tool Calling | `openai/gpt-4-turbo` |
| Cost-Effective | `minimaxai/minimax-m2` |

### 5. Streaming (Not Supported)

This endpoint does **not** support streaming responses. For real-time streaming:
- Use OpenRouter's streaming endpoint directly from frontend
- Or implement server-sent events (SSE) wrapper

